WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:25.000
In this walkthrough, we'll install BlackBox on Windows, record a local mock app, and inspect the recording in the BlackBox UI.
Download the blackbox-windows-installer artifact from GitHub Actions run 44885626025 (commit 72398c8).

00:25.000 --> 00:55.000
Extract the ZIP and run BlackBox-Setup-0.1.0.dev0.exe.
Because the preview installer is unsigned, Windows may show an unknown-publisher warning. Only proceed if you trust this build.

00:55.000 --> 01:25.000
Launch BlackBox from the Start menu or installer. On first run with no recordings, it opens the setup view.

01:25.000 --> 01:55.000
Open PowerShell, point $bb at $env:LOCALAPPDATA\Programs\BlackBox\python\python.exe, and run & $bb -m blackbox --version.

01:55.000 --> 02:35.000
Create BlackBox-Test and run mock_test.py. The mock server binds only to 127.0.0.1. No real OpenAI request is made.

02:35.000 --> 03:05.000
Run & $bb -m blackbox ls and & $bb -m blackbox verify capsules\*.bbx from the same folder.

03:05.000 --> 03:50.000
Run & $bb -m blackbox desktop from BlackBox-Test. Open the recording, click Check this capsule, and view Diagnose / Brief.

03:50.000 --> 04:15.000
Summary: unsigned Windows preview installed, local loopback mock recorded, capsule verified and diagnosed. No external provider called.
